# Only the code goes to GitHub. Everything else here is huge (champions/ 12 GB of weights, data/
# 16 GB of episodes), someone else's repository (attune-subnet/, vector-orchestrator/: the GPU box
# clones its own), or local tooling (.venv/). On the GPU box the same rule keeps everything the
# pipeline downloads and writes next to vector-train/ out of git: king/, data/, cache/, run*/,
# exports/, duels/, .venv-train/, .venv-orch/, RoboTwin-Vector/.
# So a new file at the top level is ignored until it gets its own "!/name" line below.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/vector-train/
!/vector_v1.1_architecture.png
!/vector_v1.1_architecture.svg

# Inside vector-train/: Python leftovers, and weights, data or outputs written there by mistake.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv*/
*.safetensors
*.pt
*.hdf5
*.npy
*.zip
*.tmp
selftest-work/
